auth {
  mode: awsv4
}

auth:awsv4 {
  accessKeyId: {{awsAccessKeyId}}
  secretAccessKey: {{awsSecretAccessKey}}
  sessionToken: {{awsSessionToken}}
  service: lambda
  region: {{awsRegion}}
  profileName: {{awsProfile}}
}

headers {
  X-API-Key: {{apiKey}}
  X-User-Token: {{userToken}}
}

docs {
  # archive-api

  Requests run top to bottom as a flow: each one stores the ids the next needs
  as runtime variables, so nothing has to be pasted between them. Use the
  collection runner, or run folders in order.

  ## Auth

  Three independent layers, and every request needs all three - including
  `/healthz`, which needs none of the application's own checks but still sits
  behind the Function URL's IAM gate.

  1. **AWS SigV4**, set on this collection. Production's Function URL is
     `AWS_IAM`, so an unsigned request is rejected by AWS before any of this
     API's code runs - you get a bare `Forbidden` with no JSON body, which is
     how you tell it apart from this API's own errors.
  2. **`X-API-Key`**, checked in Go.
  3. **`X-User-Token`**, a Cognito access token. Deliberately not
     `Authorization`, because SigV4 signing owns that header.

  Locally there is no IAM gate, so the signature is ignored - but Bruno still
  needs the variables to exist, which is why the local environment sets
  throwaway values rather than leaving them blank.

  ## Before the first run

  Pick an environment, then for local:

  ```
  make dev-up && make dev-setup && make run
  ```

  `apiKey` matches `API_KEY` in your `.env` (`dev-key` by default).

  `userToken` is a Cognito access token, and it is the one thing this API
  cannot give you - it only verifies tokens. See
  `docs/getting-an-access-token.md`; the short version is to copy
  `archive_access_token` out of the UI's cookies, or run `make token`.

  Tokens last 12 hours. A run of `401`s that starts suddenly usually means
  yours expired.

  ## Production

  Copy the four values out of `archives-ui/.env.local`, which already holds
  working credentials for the IAM user allowed to invoke the function:
  `ARCHIVE_API_URL`, `ARCHIVE_API_KEY`, `ARCHIVE_API_ACCESS_KEY_ID`,
  `ARCHIVE_API_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY`.

  Alternatively leave the key variables empty and set `awsProfile` to an AWS
  CLI profile name, and Bruno will use that profile's credentials instead.
}
